meta {
  name: list_attendance_request
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/method/employee_app.employee_list.list_attendance_request
  body: form-urlencoded
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  limit_start: 0
  limit_page_length: 20
}

docs {
  # List Attendance Request

  Retrieves Attendance Request records for the currently logged-in employee
  (resolved from the bearer token's user), paginated and sorted by creation date descending.

  ## Authentication
  Requires a valid Bearer token. The employee is derived from the token's user, not passed in.

  ## Parameters

  | Name               | Type | Required | Description                          |
  |--------------------|------|----------|--------------------------------------|
  | limit_start        | int  | No       | Pagination offset (default `0`)      |
  | limit_page_length  | int  | No       | Page size (default `20`)             |

  ## Response

  ```json
  {
    "message": [
      {
        "name": "HR-ATT-REQ-2026-00001",
        "employee": "HR-EMP-00003",
        "employee_name": "John Doe",
        "from_date": "2026-06-01",
        "to_date": "2026-06-01",
        "from_time": "08:11:11",
        "to_time": "16:11:11",
        "reason": "Work From Home",
        "explanation": null,
        "half_day": 0,
        "status": "Open"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Notes
  - `status` is derived from `docstatus`: `0` = Open, `1` = Approved, `2` = Cancelled.
  - Returns a 404 JSON error if no Employee record is linked to the logged-in user.
}
